# Empty states (PaperCraft)

Use the shared **`EmptyStatePanel`** (`src/components/ui/EmptyStatePanel.tsx`) for every “nothing here yet” or blocking empty view — not one-off markup per page.

## Pattern

- Centered **dashed** card (`pc-empty-panel`)
- **Icon** in soft primary-tinted square (56×56)
- **Serif title** (20px), sans body copy (13px)
- Optional **numbered steps** (left-aligned inside card)
- **Actions**: primary `pc-btn is-primary is-sm` + secondary ghost `pc-btn is-sm`
- Optional `hint` line in muted 11px text
- `variant="error"` for load failures (solid danger border, not dashed)

## When empty, hide header CTAs

If the page header has a “New …” button, show it only when the list has items (see `PapersListPage`, `BookmarksWorkspace`).

## Do not

- Build custom empty boxes with solid borders only on one module
- Use different icon sizes/title fonts per feature
- Duplicate empty-state CSS in module stylesheets — extend `styles/empty-state.css` if needed

## Examples

- Paper Library, Bookmarks, Repository filter empty → `EmptyStatePanel`
